  "answer": "I'll start by reading the project skill and locating how storefront cart endpoints and merchant settings work.The cart writes all go through one facade, and the max is read from merchant configuration on each request so a change applies without a restart. I'll reject quantities above that limit before the cart is saved.The storefront cart REST API now rejects a line quantity above the store's `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY` merchant setting (99 when that key is missing) with HTTP 400, and it does so before the cart is saved. The check runs on each request in `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl` for create, add, and quantity changes (`POST /api/v1/cart`, `PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}`, and `POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi`), including when an add is merged into an existing line. A quantity of 0 still removes the line. A non-numeric configuration value is treated as missing and falls back to 99.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 responses and that the cart is left unchanged, because the cart integration tests were not executed\"], \"missing\": [\"a unit or integration test that sets CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY and calls the cart endpoints with a quantity above and below the limit\"]}",
